</div>

</div>

<p style="margin-top:10px;">
If several answers are "no," investigate before spending hours on the application.
</p>

</div>


<div class="side-card">

<h3>⚠️ Common Time Wasters</h3>

<div class="mistake">
<strong>Applying because the award is large</strong>
<p>Large awards can require substantial preparation. Evaluate fit before value alone.</p>
</div>

<div class="mistake">
<strong>Ignoring eligibility details</strong>
<p>Read the complete requirements before writing.</p>
</div>

<div class="mistake">
<strong>Using the same essay everywhere</strong>
<p>Reuse experiences, not necessarily the entire essay.</p>
</div>

<div class="mistake">
<strong>Starting the night before</strong>
<p>Recommendations and documents often take time to obtain.</p>
</div>

<div class="mistake">
<strong>Searching only once</strong>
<p>Scholarship opportunities appear across different seasons and organizations.</p>
</div>

</div>


<div class="side-card">

<h3>📅 A Simple Weekly System</h3>

<ul class="side-list">

<li><strong>Monday:</strong> Find new opportunities.</li>

<li><strong>Tuesday:</strong> Verify eligibility.</li>

<li><strong>Wednesday:</strong> Research the organization.</li>

<li><strong>Thursday:</strong> Prepare documents or evidence.</li>

<li><strong>Friday:</strong> Draft or improve an application.</li>

<li><strong>Weekend:</strong> Review deadlines and update your tracker.</li>

</ul>

<p style="margin-top:10px;">
You don't have to follow these exact days. The important principle is separating <strong>searching, evaluating, preparing, and applying</strong> so the entire process doesn't become a last-minute scramble.
</p>

</div>


<div class="side-card">

<h3>🔁 The Compounding Strategy</h3>

<p>
Your first application may take a long time because you're building everything from scratch.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:8px;">
The second becomes easier.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:8px;">
The tenth can be dramatically more efficient because you have a resume, stories, evidence, documents, research notes, and a better understanding of your own strengths.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:8px;font-weight:700;color:#4A2F18;">
The objective is not to write more applications forever. It is to build a system that makes each future application better and more efficient.
</p>

</div>


